      en: 'The thyroid is a butterfly-shaped endocrine gland at the front of the neck, below the larynx and wrapped around the windpipe. It releases hormones that set the pace of metabolism in every cell of the body, and behind it sit four small parathyroid glands that regulate calcium.'
