      en: 'A transverse section showing the three cylindrical bodies: two corpora cavernosa above and a corpus spongiosum below carrying the urethra in its centre. Each corpus cavernosum is enclosed by a tough fibrous sheath, the tunica albuginea, with a deep artery running in its core to supply the erectile tissue. Dorsally, veins, arteries and nerves run together in one bundle, and the whole is wrapped by deep fascia, then subcutaneous fat, then skin.'
