      en: 'Carrying urine from the bladder to the exterior through the urethral lumen held within the corpus spongiosum, supplying the erectile tissue with blood through the deep arteries and draining it through the dorsal veins. The tunica albuginea maintains the shape of the erectile bodies and resists over-distension, and the dorsal nerves carry sensation from the skin and the deeper tissues.'
