      en: 'The knee is the largest and most weight-bearing joint in the body. The lower end of the femur meets the upper end of the tibia here, with the patella gliding in front. Its stability does not come from the shape of the bones, since their surfaces are nearly flat, but from the ligaments, the menisci and the surrounding muscles, which is why it is so often injured in sport. The joint is shown here opened from the front with the patella turned downward.'
